<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch adj. unemployment seen a bit lower.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch adj. unemployment seen a bit lower.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank economists expect figures due on Wednesday to show a slight drop in seasonally adjusted Dutch unemployment for the three months to November. Their forecasts are summarised below</p>
<p> GMT   Date  Period   Indicator	   Consensus  Range    Pvs</p>
<p> 0830 18/12  Sep-Nov  Unemployment NSA  438,000    434-441  438</p>
<p> 0830 18/12  Sep-Nov  Unemployment SA   438,000    434-442  442</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, ING, IRIS, Generale Bank, MeesPierson, Rabobank.</p>
<p>NOTE - NSA = non-seasonally adjusted, SA = seas. adjusted.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
